export anchor TerminalLightStyle:
    number: 14
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Terminal light
    idea: A light terminal session on warm cream, where everything is monospace, panels are drawn with box lines and progress is a row of hash marks.
    base: light
    palette:
        cream: #fdf6e3, the page
        bar: #eee8d5, the top status line and the bottom key bar
        ink: #2b2a26, text, box lines, the primary button fill and the cursor block
        dim: #5c5a50, meta text, column headers and the hollow cells of last week's chart
        rule: #a59f8c, dot leaders and dashed rules
        blue: #1d4f91, links and the filled cells of this week's chart
        plum: #8a2f6b, key hints in brackets, user handles and heading markers
        ok: #2f6a00, the [+] ON TRACK code and the user at host part of the prompt
        warn: #8a5200, the [!] AT RISK code
        bad: #b0221c, the [x] BEHIND code and the overdue count
        sel: #f5e7b8, the selected row and the focus fill
    type:
        One monospace stack for everything, ui-monospace, SF Mono,
        JetBrains Mono, Menlo, Consolas, DejaVu Sans Mono, Liberation Mono,
        monospace, with tabular figures. Body is 14px at 1.5 line height,
        13px on phones. Panel titles and status codes are 14px bold.
        Column headers are 14px regular capitals in the dim colour. The
        style sheet title is 20px bold. There are no other sizes.
    layout:
        A tmux style status line runs across the top with a plum square
        and the lowercase wordmark, the nav as numbered windows such as
        0 home and 1 projects with the current one bold, underlined and
        starred, and the user name on the right. Below it sits the prompt
        line mara at brightwork ~ $ dashboard with a solid block cursor,
        then a row with the search box, the new project button and the
        notify(3) button, each showing its key hint. A double lined
        greeting box holds the greeting and the overdue warning. Then a
        two column grid holds the summary box beside the chart box, and the
        projects table and the activity log each span the full width. A key
        bar of shortcuts closes the page. Content is capped at 1240px.
        Below 860px everything is one column, and the table scrolls inside
        its box.
    spacing: Character grid. A 1ch horizontal unit, an 8px vertical unit, 16px between panels and 20px top padding inside a box.
    density: Medium high. One record per line, with no cards.
    corners: None anywhere. Everything is square.
    borders:
        Every panel is a 1px ink box with its lowercase title cut into the
        top edge between box drawing tees, and an optional dim hint or
        link cut into the top right edge. The greeting box uses a 3px
        double line. Table headers sit over a dashed ink line, and the
        summary uses dotted leaders between each label and its value.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        No pictograms at all. Status is a bracket code and a capital word,
        [+] ON TRACK, [!] AT RISK and [x] BEHIND. Progress is ten
        characters of hash marks and dashes in brackets followed by the
        percent. Key hints such as [n], [/] and [o] appear in plum. The
        chart is columns of small cells, hollow for last week and filled
        blue for this week, with the value above each column and the day
        letter below.
    focus: A 2px dashed ink outline offset 2px with the sel fill. The primary button keeps its ink fill and takes the outline offset 3px.
    tone: Lowercase command words, such as tail -f activity, ls -a, notify(3) and grep. Full sentences appear only in the greeting.
